      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Basically what is sad is that the runtime implementation could very easily keep track of it's previous value it generated and then use that to check its current value to see if it is the same with such an option checked simply by doing something like: \"if (_prevValue == currentValue) // redo the rand until a different number is generated.\" (with 4~6 lines of added runtime code not including the if statement brackets).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
