  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-06-19T03:37:12.563Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently in my Avatar I use a local only random component that sets a synced rand param on 2 layers. Sadly this results in me needing to duplicate these params for storing the previous value it generated after I use the value to transition to another state which also checks this previous value to prevent the transition if it is the exact same number. Issue is however is this wastes 16 synced (or non-synced) bits that I would rather avoid by having this feature in the parameter driver itself that shows up as a check box when someone selects to use a Random type number for a parameter. This could also help optimize a lot of existing assets for avatars as well. SDK version: latest stable 3.8.1\n\nExample:\n\nSay that one wants to generate Random number between 1 and 8.\n\nExpected Result: 1, 5, 4, 3, ... (never consecutive same number)\n\nCurrent Possible Result: 1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 3, 3, ... (it could potentially repeat).",
